  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file list for the Spring Kafka listener container threading refactor across all three repos, ordered most important first:\n\n**spring-kafka** (primary implementation, most changes):\n- `AbstractMessageListenerContainer.java`, `ConcurrentMessageListenerContainer.java`, `KafkaMessageListenerContainer.java` \u2014 the core threading model classes (single-threaded container, its concurrent wrapper spawning N single-threaded children)\n- `ContainerProperties.java`, `ConsumerProperties.java` \u2014 carry the `AsyncTaskExecutor`/`TaskScheduler` config threaded through both container types\n- `MessageListenerContainer.java`, `GenericMessageListenerContainer.java`, `ListenerContainerRegistry.java` \u2014 the interfaces both container types implement\n- `config/ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactory.java`, `AbstractKafkaListenerContainerFactory.java`, `KafkaListenerContainerFactory.java`, `ContainerCustomizer.java`, `AbstractKafkaListenerEndpoint.java`, `KafkaListenerEndpoint.java`, `KafkaListenerEndpointRegistry.java` \u2014 factory/registry layer that constructs and manages container lifecycle (registry checks `SmartLifecycle` phase consistency across containers)\n- `annotation/EnableKafka.java`, `KafkaListener.java`, `KafkaBootstrapConfiguration.java` \u2014 annotation-driven bootstrapping that wires endpoints to factories\n- Existing tests (`ConcurrentMessageListenerContainerTests.java`, `...MockTests.java`) \u2014 must be extended for any concurrency-model change\n\n**spring-boot** (consumer, autoconfigures the factory):\n- `KafkaAnnotationDrivenConfiguration.java` \u2014 creates the `ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactory` bean\n- `ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactoryConfigurer.java` \u2014 maps `spring.kafka.listener.concurrency` property onto the factory\n- `KafkaProperties.java` \u2014 owns the `Listener.concurrency` property\n- `KafkaAutoConfiguration.java` \u2014 top-level autoconfiguration importing the above\n\n**spring-framework** (upstream abstractions consumed by spring-kafka's threading model):\n- `AsyncTaskExecutor.java`, `TaskExecutor.java`, `SimpleAsyncTaskExecutor.java` \u2014 the executor abstraction each concurrent child container thread runs on\n- `SmartLifecycle.java`, `Lifecycle.java` \u2014 the phased start/stop contract every container and the `KafkaListenerEndpointRegistry` implement\n\nThis confirms the dependency chain you described: spring-framework's `TaskExecutor`/`SmartLifecycle` are consumed unchanged by spring-kafka's container classes, spring-kafka's `ConcurrentMessageListenerContainer`/`ContainerProperties` surface is what spring-boot's autoconfiguration binds `spring.kafka.listener.concurrency` onto, so refactor order should flow framework \u2192 kafka \u2192 boot, with boot's changes gated on the kafka API being stable (its configurer touches `setConcurrency`, `getContainerProperties()`, and the `AsyncTaskExecutor` setter directly).",
